{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14958 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between cis-5-Dodecenoic acid and DNA polymerase iota, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with DNA polymerase iota. The compound directly targets LS174T, a protein that is a known target of several other molecules, including [(1S,3S,4R,9R,10S,13S)-5,5,9-trimethyl-14-methylidene-11,15-dioxo-3-tetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9]hexadecanyl] acetate and (3E,4S)-3-[2-[(1R,4aS,6R,8aS)-6-hydroxy-5,8a-dimethyl-2-methylidene-5-[[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]-3,4,4a,6,7,8-hexahydro-1H-naphthalen-1-yl]ethylidene]-4-hydroxyoxolan-2-one. These molecules are likely acting through similar mechanisms, possibly by modulating the activity of LS174T, which in turn influences DNA polymerase iota. The consistent presence of LS174T as a target and its subsequent interaction with DNA polymerase iota suggests a well-defined pathway, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible, biologically relevant relationship, but further investigation is needed to confirm the precise mode of action and therapeutic potential.",
